  "summary_en": "Pyro Advect moves the contents of VDB volumes along a velocity VDB, the core step for transporting smoke or fire in a Pyro simulation. It can also advect the velocity field itself, or skip that step when another Pyro Advect already did it.",
  "inputs": [
    "data: cable of all the VDBs to advect",
    "v: vector VDB driving the advection, which can optionally be self-advected"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Scale: global multiplier on velocity values",
    "Ambient Velocity: constant global velocity added to the advection, usable as a wind effect",
    "Scale by Timestep: scales velocity by the timestep",
    "Trace Method: integration scheme per trace step, from Forward Euler (fastest, most diffusion) to Runge-Kutta 4 (most accurate, most expensive)",
    "Path Tracing: several trace steps to follow curved paths, preserving fine detail and vortices",
    "Maximum Steps: cap on path-tracing steps",
    "CFL Condition: approximate voxels stepped per trace step; lower is more stable but slower",
    "Adaptive Step Size: adjusts the step size dynamically",
    "Enable Data Advection / Scheme: BFECC, Euler + Sharpen or Euler; BFECC preserves sharpness best but costs the most",
    "Sharpen: counters diffusion; values that are too high cause grid artifacts",
    "Enable Velocity Advection / Method: self-advection of the velocity VDB and its scheme; can be turned off if another node already advected it",
    "Outputs: the advected data VDBs and the velocity VDB"
  ],
  "caveats": [
